The query in `2result.sql` is safest:

• It first isolates the earliest five topic IDs in a CTE, then calculates the metrics only for those rows, guaranteeing that exactly five topics are reported.  
• It groups by `t."Id"` (the primary key) so different topics that happen to share the same title/creation date cannot be merged accidentally (unlike `0result.sql`).  
• All counts are wrapped in `COALESCE`, and `TotalViews` is handled likewise, fully satisfying the “treat NULL as 0” requirement.  

The other two files either miss grouping by the topic id or rely on ordering/limiting after aggregation, which can return fewer or improperly‑combined rows.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```